{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Two hundred goats, etc.</b> I heard from my master, my elder, the righteous and holy one, of blessed memory, that Jacob intended with the calculation of the animals he sent a tally corresponding to Seir's numerical value, which is 482, and therefore he sent in calculated measure: goats and ewes 440, and camels thirty with their young, which are sixty — that makes 500; cows and bulls fifty, donkeys and their young thirty — that makes 482 — to break his strength."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "ת״מ resolved as 440 (ת״מ = ת״מ); ת״ק resolved as 500 (ת״ק); תק״ף resolved as 482 (תק״ף), the gematria of שֵׂעִיר. The phrase לִשְׁבֹּר תָּקְפּוֹ is rendered 'to break his strength,' reading תָּקְפּוֹ as 'his strength/power.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:37.852168892Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}